.TH tunotesdb n 0.1 tclutils
.SH "tclutils::tunotesdb — SQLite\-backed note store"
.PP
The persistent counterpart to \fBtunotes\fR. Same note layout, so both engines are interchangeable and \fBtkutils::tkunotes\fR works with either.
.CS
package require sqlite3
package require tclutils::tunotesdb 0.1

sqlite3 db notes.db
tclutils::tunotesdb::init db

set id [tclutils::tunotesdb::create db "Build notes" "litehtml with nmake" {build}]
foreach hit [tclutils::tunotesdb::search db nmake] {
    puts "[dict get $hit title]: [dict get $hit snippet]"
}
.CE
.SS "Which of the two engines"
.TS
l l l.
	\fBtunotes\fR	\fBtunotesdb\fR
Storage	one Tcl dict, saved as JSON	one row per note in SQLite
Saving	rewrites the whole file	transactional, per note
Search	linear \fBstring match\fR	FTS5 index, ranked, with snippets
Hierarchy	walked in Tcl	\fBWITH RECURSIVE\fR in the database
Dependencies	none	\fBsqlite3\fR (FTS5)
Good for	a handful of notes, no extra packages	many notes, several writers, a server
.TE
.PP
The note dict is identical in both:
.CS
id parent_id title content created modified tags
.CE
.PP
\fBparent_id\fR is the empty string for a root note; \fBtags\fR is a Tcl list; timestamps are \fB%Y\-%m\-%d %H:%M:%S\fR, as in \fBtunotes\fR.
.SS "Opening the database"
.PP
Like \fBtusqlite\fR, this module does \fBnot\fR \fBpackage require sqlite3\fR itself — the caller opens the database and passes the handle. That keeps the module sourceable anywhere and leaves the choice of file, flags and lifetime with the application.
.SS "\fBinit db\fR"
.PP
Creates the schema if it is not there yet and switches the database to WAL, so readers do not block the writer. Safe to call on every start.
.PP
The full\-text index is an FTS5 table with \fBcontent='notes'\fR: it does not store the text a second time, and three triggers keep it in step with the table — no application code has to remember to reindex. \fBinit\fR raises \fBNOFTS5\fR if the SQLite build has no FTS5 (part of the standard build since 3.9).
.SS Commands
.PP
All commands are also reachable through the ensemble \fBtclutils::tunotesdb\fR.
.SS Notes
.TS
l l.
Command	Returns
\fBcreate db title content ?tags? ?parentId?\fR	the new id
\fBupdate db id title content ?tags? ?parentId?\fR	the id; \fBparentId\fR defaults to \fBKEEP\fR
\fBget db id\fR	the note dict
\fBexists db id\fR	boolean
\fBdelete db id ?cascade?\fR	—; with \fBcascade\fR (default 1) the subtree goes, without it the children become roots
\fBmove db id newParentId\fR	the id; refuses cycles
\fBids db\fR / \fBcount db\fR	all ids / how many
.TE
.SS Hierarchy
.TS
l l.
Command	Returns
\fBroots db\fR	ids without a parent
\fBchildren db parentId\fR	direct children (\fB""\fR for the roots)
\fBdescendants db id\fR	everything below, depth\-first
\fBancestors db id\fR	from the parent up to the root
\fBparent db id\fR	the parent id, \fB""\fR for a root
\fBpath db id\fR	root first, the note itself last
\fBdepth db id\fR	0 for a root
\fBsiblings db id\fR	the other children of the same parent
\fBsubtree db id\fR	the note plus everything below
.TE
.PP
The tree lives in \fBparent_id\fR and is walked with \fBWITH RECURSIVE\fR. The work stays in the database instead of loading every note to follow a chain of parents.
.SS Search
.CS
search db query ?-limit N? ?-snippet N?
.CE
.PP
Returns a list of dicts with the keys \fBid\fR, \fBtitle\fR, \fBsnippet\fR and \fBrank\fR, best match first. \fB\-limit\fR defaults to 50 (\fB0\fR for all), \fB\-snippet\fR to 10 words of context.
.PP
The query goes to FTS5, so its syntax applies:
.TS
l l.
Query	Meaning
\fBnmake\fR	the word
\fBalpha beta\fR	both words (AND)
\fB"exact phrase"\fR	literally
\fBconfig*\fR	prefix
\fBalpha OR beta\fR, \fBalpha NOT beta\fR	as written
.TE
.PP
A syntactically wrong query raises \fBBADQUERY\fR rather than returning nothing — a typo should not look like an empty result.
.SS Tags
.PP
\fBbyTag db tag\fR returns the ids carrying the tag, \fBtags db\fR every tag in use, sorted and without duplicates. Tags are stored as a Tcl list in one column and compared in Tcl, so a tag containing a space stays one tag.
.SS "Bridge to tunotes"
.TS
l l.
Command	Purpose
\fBtoStore db\fR	the whole database as a \fBtunotes\fR store
\fBfromStore db store ?\-clear 1?\fR	import a \fBtunotes\fR store; returns how many notes
.TE
.PP
\fBtoStore\fR hands the data to code that expects the in\-memory engine — including \fBtclutils::tunotes::toJson\fR for a JSON export. \fBfromStore\fR runs in one transaction: a failure half\-way leaves the database as it was.
.SS Errors
.PP
\fBerrorCode\fR is always \fB{TCLUTILS TUNOTESDB <REASON>}\fR:
.TS
l l.
Reason	When
\fBNODB\fR	the handle is not a usable sqlite3 command
\fBNOFTS5\fR	SQLite without FTS5
\fBNOTFOUND\fR	no note with that id, or no such parent
\fBCYCLE\fR	a move would put a note under itself or a descendant
\fBBADQUERY\fR	FTS5 could not parse the search query
\fBBADOPTION\fR	unknown option, or an unusable \fB\-limit\fR
\fBBADNOTE\fR	a note handed to \fBfromStore\fR is missing a field
.TE
.SS Requirements
.PP
Tcl 8.6 or later, \fBtclutils::tusqlite\fR, and an \fBsqlite3\fR package with FTS5 at the point of use. Tested against SQLite 3.45 (Tcl 8.6) and 3.53 (Tcl 9.0).
